1
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:12,387
[intriguing music playing]

2
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:15,015
[Ella] I think it really gives
the adventure Josh is looking for.

3
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:17,350
[Imogen] He'll love it.
Absolutely love it.

4
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,060
Yay! Great.

5
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:21,479
I really dig
the funeral parlor vibes here.

6
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:23,648
It was my grandparents' house.

7
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:27,068
Hey, do they haunt the place,
or is it just the curtains?

8
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:30,196
[Ella] Hey, Josh,
what kind of cake were you thinking?

9
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,240
Anything but cupcakes.

10
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,325
-Smart man.
-[Josh laughs]

11
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:35,410
Your mom likes me.

12
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:39,372
She also likes Phil Collins and pastels.
It's a low bar.

13
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:41,082
[phone buzzes]

14
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:43,251
Britney?

15
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,171
Uh… Crew thing.

16
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:47,964
What?

17
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:50,800
That's weird, I didn't get one.

18
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,846
There's another group text?

19
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:58,058
You're the other group text, Coxie.
Just figuring that out?

20
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:03,480
Oh, and the dinner
with Josh's grandfather.

21
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:07,776
At a restaurant run by an old friend
who just got her first Michelin star.

22
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,778
You guys are gonna love the food.

23
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:12,030
-It sounds amazing.
-[Ella chuckles]

24
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:15,325
You have a very beautiful home,
Miss Emerson.

25
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,243
Nice to see you again, Teagan.

26
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:18,369
-Bye.
-Bye-bye.

27
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:20,205
Bye.

28
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:22,248
-[Ella] Bye!
-[door closes]

29
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:25,877
What a well-mannered young man.

30
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:28,463
What?

31
00:01:28,546 --> 00:01:34,469
["Ten Girls" by Circe playing]

32
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,810
{\an8}Hey, plan for warm-up today?

33
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:43,853
{\an8}Pick drills on the erg.

34
00:01:43,937 --> 00:01:46,898
{\an8}Everyone's posture is fine
for the first K, but then it falls apart.

35
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:48,858
{\an8}I think we need to rework the basics.

36
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:51,653
{\an8}And how's Ryder holding up in stroke?

37
00:01:51,736 --> 00:01:53,655
{\an8}Good. But he knows it.

38
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:54,656
[laughs]

39
00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:56,241
So keep an eye on that.

40
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:59,035
You've managed to get a handle on
this team in a few weeks.

41
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,787
You just might whip them into shape.

42
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,832
One thing, though. Where are they?

43
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:12,257
All right, that's the last of the fries.
Uh, cheese.

44
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:15,552
Hey. Is anyone coming?

45
00:02:16,052 --> 00:02:17,387
Coast is clear.

46
00:02:18,388 --> 00:02:21,641
Ryder intercepted Mr. Wu,
and Baloo's side is good too.

47
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:24,686
But the question remains,
do we need to be doing this?

48
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:26,729
Yeah, Quaid,
what did this kid do to you anyway?

49
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:30,024
To me, nothing. But he's shaking down
the freshman on the novice team.

50
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:33,444
He's making him buy them loaded fries
at the commissary every day.

51
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:34,821
Beef.

52
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:38,366
So as payback,
we're giving him all the loaded fries.

53
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:41,077
Dude needs to be sent a message.

54
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:44,581
Everyone else is too scared to do it,
so it has to be us. Gravy.

55
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:47,458
Hang on, hang on. Incoming, incoming.
It's Principal Cabrera's grandkid.

56
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,668
Yeah, that makes sense.

57
00:02:48,751 --> 00:02:50,420
-This is his car.
-Quaid!

58
00:02:50,503 --> 00:02:51,671
-What?
-What?

59
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,091
What the hell are you doing to my car?

60
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:56,843
-Run!
-[Noah] Let's go!

61
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:57,927
[Cam] Come on!

62
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:59,846
["Gosports!!!" by couchgagzzz playing]

63
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:00,930
[boy] Quaid!

64
00:03:03,057 --> 00:03:05,059
-Morning!
-Morning, morning, morning!

65
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:06,811
[guitar playing off-key]

66
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:07,896
[Quaid] Whoo!

67
00:03:07,979 --> 00:03:09,022
You're flat!

68
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:14,235
Hey, sweet sack, bro!

69
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,738
Hey, she could do better!

70
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:20,283
Hello, boys.

71
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:21,826
Running late?

72
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:26,372
[song ends]

73
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:30,418
Detention? Instead of practice?

74
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:35,506
Did we forget the Head of the Laurence
Regatta is coming up?

75
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,467
Are we supposed
to hand it over to Westvale now?

76
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,260
Hope it was worth it.

77
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:41,596
Quaid! With me.

78
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:45,934
As for the rest of you,
you've been assigned essays.

79
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,435
Get to work.

80
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,231
[sullen music playing]

81
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:52,440
Stay.

82
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:54,776
Now you know where your rowers are.

83
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:05,119
Not the first student
to try and bully the principal's grandson.

84
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:06,788
I wasn't bullying him.

85
00:04:06,871 --> 00:04:09,540
I believe the interior of Ethan's car
tells a different story.

86
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:10,500
[snickers]

87
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:13,461
Is that amusing to you, Mr. Quaid?

88
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:16,089
You've shown a pattern
of disruptive behavior

89
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:17,674
that has no place at Easton.

90
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:20,260
-Maybe you should look at Ethan.
-Ethan is the victim here.

91
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:21,511
You're out of chances.

92
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:24,430
I think…
we need to look at the big picture here.

93
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:27,809
All right? Quaid's a good kid.
He gives 100% on the team.

94
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:30,770
-Yes, he messed up.
-No, I didn't.

95
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,150
-I did.
-And he will never do it again.

96
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:38,987
As a matter of fact,
he's gonna keep his head down,

97
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,781
write his essay, and work really hard

98
00:04:41,864 --> 00:04:44,575
so he can be in our boat
for our big regatta.

99
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:55,837
I'm sorry. I know I was wrong.
And I swear I won't do it again.

100
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:00,300
[Baloo] Hey, Perry.

101
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:03,428
What's your hack
for looking so good in photos?

102
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,222
Always be alpha.

103
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:08,850
No, I'm not into toxic masculinity.

104
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:11,311
No, me? Toxic masculine?

105
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:18,359
No, it's short form. ALPHA.
Angles, Lighting, Posture, Hair, Attitude.

106
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,028
Who's the pic for?

107
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:24,157
This guy I'm texting.
Boy's been generous with thirsty snaps,

108
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,993
and now he wants some back,
and I've got nothing.

109
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:30,455
Seriously? Even my grandma's got,
like, one emergency thirst trap.

110
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:34,876
Every time I try to take some,
I feel like an idiot. I'm more IRL sexy.

111
00:05:34,959 --> 00:05:36,669
I'll hook you up with my ring light.

112
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,504
Once you get the vibes
and the lighting going,

113
00:05:38,588 --> 00:05:39,422
can't go wrong.

114
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:43,009
First, obligatory family dinner party
for Granddad.

115
00:05:43,092 --> 00:05:45,053
Right. "Thank you for the life of luxury."

116
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:48,014
-Then, it's time for the real party.
-[knocks on table]

117
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:49,349
Listen up, boys.

118
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:54,437
Y'all are invited to my young, rich,
and depraved birthday weekend.

119
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:56,898
Starting with Formula 1 go-karts racing.

120
00:05:56,981 --> 00:06:00,151
-Sick.
-Then, MMA lessons and cage match.

121
00:06:00,234 --> 00:06:02,653
Because Ryder needs some practice.

122
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:06,824
-Baller.
-And finally, the private jet to Atlanta.

123
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:09,202
Because we're all going to see Kendrick.

124
00:06:09,285 --> 00:06:11,496
-[all exclaiming and whooping]
-[Perry] Get it on!

125
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:13,414
Yeah!

126
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:17,251
Going to Josh's party?
You're not even friends.

127
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:19,587
-It's a team thing.
-Mm-hmm.

128
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:22,340
And the team thing means
getting roped into Quaid's juvenile stunt

129
00:06:22,423 --> 00:06:23,424
and getting detention?

130
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:25,134
Yeah, I know. It's immature,

131
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,678
but he's like a little brother.
I'd be a dick if I didn't.

132
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,890
If you say so.

133
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:35,770
-Have you never been on a team before?
-Uh, yeah. Swimming, tennis, track.

134
00:06:35,853 --> 00:06:37,063
Those are solo sports.

135
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:38,106
What's your point?

136
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:40,191
Somebody never learned
to play well with others.

137
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:43,820
[laughing] Hey, I'm a better team player
than everyone else on the crew.

138
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:45,780
So we'll work on that.

139
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,369
-I'm back.
-[all cheering and exclaiming]

140
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:55,039
All right, all right, all right.
But he's on his last strike.

141
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,582
One slip and he's off the team.

142
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:01,170
Let this be a warning to all of you.
Behave yourself.

143
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:10,346
Oh, Quaid, hey.

144
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:14,934
I just wanna talk. Coxie to rower.

145
00:07:15,601 --> 00:07:19,147
There can't be any more
of these childish pranks, okay?

146
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:20,398
Paybacks.

147
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:23,860
-Here, sorry, could you hold these?
-I know you think everything's a big joke.

148
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:27,029
But, hey, you are
a big part of our engine room.

149
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:29,198
We can't lose you, so pull it together.

150
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:31,325
No more of these pay…backs.

151
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:34,245
-Aye, aye, Captain.
-Why are you putting eggs in your bag?

152
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:37,039
Not my bag.

153
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:38,249
Huh?

154
00:07:38,332 --> 00:07:40,585
[mischievous music playing]

155
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:43,129
-Quaid!
-[quietly] No, come on!

156
00:07:43,212 --> 00:07:44,922
-Ugh!
-[whispers] Get over here!

157
00:07:53,055 --> 00:07:56,601
We just got out of detention.
What the hell were you thinking?

158
00:07:57,185 --> 00:08:02,356
I'm sorry. I know I was wrong,
and I swear I won't do it again.

159
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:07,612
[jet engine roaring]

160
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:11,741
Welcome to the Death Star.

161
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:15,786
I've always wondered
what Granddad's office looked like.

162
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:16,913
Impressive.

163
00:08:16,996 --> 00:08:18,372
[Richard] I was nervous, too,

164
00:08:18,456 --> 00:08:20,958
when I was first called into head office
on my birthday.

165
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,669
That's when my grandfather was CEO.

166
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,506
It's another Regis rite of passage.

167
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:30,218
Great Uncle Sterling is a VP,
and he's getting on.

168
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:31,928
His office could be yours one day.

169
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,057
Josh.

170
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:39,560
-You hear me?
-Yeah. I'm ready.

171
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:43,022
Just remember,
Granddad expects our family to lead.

172
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:45,399
This is your future, son.

173
00:08:46,734 --> 00:08:50,655
Josh. Richard. Thanks for coming in.

174
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:57,245
I called you in today
because I'm looking to train a new VP,

175
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,329
starting now.

176
00:08:58,412 --> 00:08:59,705
You can count on me.

177
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,042
Not everyone is cut out to be a leader.

178
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:05,253
Requires a certain skill set.

179
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:07,922
When I think about it,
everything I needed to learn as a leader,

180
00:09:08,005 --> 00:09:09,715
I learned from rowing.

181
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:14,595
As the stroke seat. In stroke,
you have to follow your own rhythm,

182
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:17,473
ignore the pull of the crew,
and set the winning pace.

183
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:21,143
Josh has been in the eight seat
since he started at Easton.

184
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:24,605
[grandfather] Mm-hmm.

185
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:30,027
As a CEO, you must always do
what's best for the company.

186
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:31,404
Of course.

187
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:35,366
So how do you know
when you have the best candidate?

188
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:36,325
[tense music playing]

189
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:37,577
Uh…

190
00:09:39,078 --> 00:09:40,705
When it beats the competition.

191
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:43,040
Come in.

192
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:48,254
Josh, starting this summer,
you'll be interning with Uncle Sterling.

193
00:09:48,337 --> 00:09:52,049
And joining you will be Ryder,
the current stroke seat.

194
00:09:54,385 --> 00:09:56,053
Glad to be on board.

195
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:11,861
Okay, birthday boy.
I flew in your favorite. Nobu.

196
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:15,865
Black cod miso, Wagyu dumplings, and…

197
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:19,493
Babe, are you okay?

198
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:22,913
Uh… No, I'm not.

199
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,585
It's just more of Regis drama.

200
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,837
Drama is what our families are all about.

201
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:31,881
What's up?

202
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,009
I think I just got demoted.

203
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:37,553
I'm supposed to train
to take over the family business,

204
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:39,639
but now my grandfather
wants it to be Ryder.

205
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,432
-Then get it back.
-How?

206
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:43,142
You know your grandfather. You tell me.

207
00:10:44,101 --> 00:10:47,313
I have to get back in the stroke seat,
but that's gonna take time.

208
00:10:47,396 --> 00:10:48,773
So you need something now.

209
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:51,275
-[ominous music playing]
-What other card do you have to play?

210
00:10:51,817 --> 00:10:53,069
[exhales]

211
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,491
Wait. He's coming to my birthday party.

212
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:01,369
Yeah, I could, um…

213
00:11:01,452 --> 00:11:03,537
I could invite the board
and get their support.

214
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:05,915
Show Granddad
that I'm a better leader than Ryder.

215
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:09,043
Not with "young, rich, and depraved,"
you won't.

216
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:10,127
No.

217
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,171
But I know what will.

218
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:13,297
[giggles demurely]

219
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,593
Why can't I do my homework
with the other guys?

220
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:21,472
Because you can't be trusted.
Now, just finish that problem.

221
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:24,725
[Teagan sighs]

222
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:27,728
Babysitting sucks.

223
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,522
That's why I let you raise yourself.

224
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:32,274
Help me choose a flavor
for Josh's birthday.

225
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:34,735
Which one tastes like privilege?

226
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:36,320
Coconut white chocolate.

227
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,905
[laughing]

228
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:39,990
Can't believe you're suddenly
an event planner.

229
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:40,908
[knocking on door]

230
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:46,122
What are you talking about?
I have thrown hundreds of parties.

231
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:48,499
Yeah, thrown, not planned.

232
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:51,919
Mom, when my old rowing club asked you
to bring food to the last regatta,

233
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:53,379
you doordashed it last at the minute.

234
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:57,049
Yeah. And those tortas were crazy good.
You're welcome.

235
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:01,303
Josh, Imogen.

236
00:12:01,387 --> 00:12:02,763
Josh is here?

237
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:03,723
Quaid, come on.

238
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:06,100
-[makes shooting noises]
-No, focus.

239
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:08,394
I was just
putting some finishing details--

240
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:11,105
Oh, don't worry about that.
There is a new plan.

241
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:12,106
There is?

242
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:15,401
It is gonna be a tribute
to the history of Regis Airlines.

243
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:18,195
We need to invite the board,
our top shareholders,

244
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,364
Easton's rowing committee.
My mom's got a list.

245
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:24,535
Okay, so there… Uh, a new theme.

246
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:28,247
This looks like triple the guest list.
And it's still in six days?

247
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:29,874
Yeah. Why wouldn't it be?

248
00:12:29,957 --> 00:12:32,126
Why don't you kids
just talk amongst yourselves

249
00:12:32,209 --> 00:12:34,128
while Ella and I go over the plans?

250
00:12:37,882 --> 00:12:38,799
We still go-karting?

251
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:41,010
-[Imogen] He wanted to tell you in person.
-No.

252
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:42,720
I know. It's a big ask,

253
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:46,265
but it's really important to my family
that this goes perfectly.

254
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:49,351
How does double your fee sound?

255
00:12:51,854 --> 00:12:53,314
Prepare for takeoff.

256
00:12:57,818 --> 00:13:00,905
In 1960, Regis Airlines had
bossa nova in their first-class lounge,

257
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:04,033
so all smooth period tunes, okay?

258
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:09,288
Wow. Mom, it's spectacular.

259
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,539
Did you just compliment me?

260
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:12,249
-[bossa nova playing]
-Don't push it.

261
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,167
[Ella exclaims]

262
00:13:13,959 --> 00:13:14,919
[Imogen] Ella.

263
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:19,256
Let me welcome you
to Regis Airlines' golden age of flight.

264
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,008
The flight attendants
will be happy to serve

265
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:22,802
the finest hors d'oeuvres
from their carts.

266
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:25,137
And the signature cocktail
is a Paper Plane.

267
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:27,264
Ooh, I love the bossa nova.

268
00:13:28,015 --> 00:13:31,519
Miss Emerson,
this is beyond what I imagined.

269
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:32,436
Sweet.

270
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,897
Thank you so much
for pulling this together.

271
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:37,233
A lovely party for a lovely young man.

272
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:38,943
I'm gonna check to see if the crew's here.

273
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:40,653
I've gotta go grab Britney.

274
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:47,117
Did you know that I'm a lovely young man?

275
00:13:47,201 --> 00:13:48,577
So was Ted Bundy.

276
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:50,538
Hm. Did I really invite you?

277
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,291
Your mom did.
She needed someone charming at the party.

278
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:58,671
I would love for you to meet my husband,
Richard Regis. This is Ella.

279
00:13:58,754 --> 00:13:59,588
Hi.

280
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:02,925
-Why do I know you?
-I used to watch you row.

281
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:04,760
I'm Matt Hayden's friend.

282
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:06,053
Right.

283
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:10,766
-You're the one that got away.
-Oh, I don't think he'd put it that way.

284
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:14,270
But I did move. And now I'm back.

285
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:18,816
Lucky him. Beautiful party.
I see some guests arriving.

286
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:22,194
Do you have enough servers?
I haven't seen any.

287
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:25,155
-Oh yeah, they'll be out shortly.
-Fantastic.

288
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:27,533
Send over some caviar bombs
as soon as they get here.

289
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:29,243
Yes, ma'am. [laughs]

290
00:14:31,495 --> 00:14:33,664
Ugh. Um…

291
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:38,502
[phone line ringing]

292
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:43,924
-[woman] <i>Hello?</i>
-Hi, it's Ella calling. Where are you?

293
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:47,011
Is this too much bulge
or not enough bulge?

294
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:48,762
I don't wanna see your nudes.

295
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:52,224
-I see enough of that in the shower.
-It's not nudes. It's implied nudity.

296
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,517
Come on, Camouflage.

297
00:14:54,018 --> 00:14:55,269
Okay.

298
00:14:55,352 --> 00:14:56,729
Help a crewman out.

299
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:59,648
Don't send me into the wild
with a subpar thirst trap.

300
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:02,651
Yeah, the rest of us voted already.
I went with the muscle shot.

301
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:05,946
-Bro looks jacked.
-I like the one that looks like a Goya.

302
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,866
It's like no one's even been to a museum.

303
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,618
Please.

304
00:15:14,496 --> 00:15:15,581
Muscles.

305
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:16,665
Thank you.

306
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,628
Okay, whoa, hold up, Q.

307
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:23,422
-You know the drill.
-It's a friend's party.

308
00:15:23,505 --> 00:15:24,548
I'm not gonna do anything.

309
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:28,260
Look.

310
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:33,223
Okay, all clear. Come on.

311
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,768
Ooh… Who gets to do the pat-down?

312
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:38,020
[girl giggles]

313
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:43,859
Yeah, no, this is where I draw the line.
No coxie blocks.

314
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:50,240
I didn't think you were coming.

315
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:53,577
Well, I'm on Quaid duty.

316
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:55,871
It's been six days without an incident.

317
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,623
That might be the longest streak yet.

318
00:15:57,706 --> 00:16:00,334
Look at you, figuring out the team thing.

319
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:09,343
This is significantly less
"young and depraved."

320
00:16:09,843 --> 00:16:13,722
I don't know. Sometimes all you need
is a dry rosé and good conversation.

321
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:15,432
Yeah, if you're a Real Housewife.

322
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:19,937
-Well, what do you think?
-Ah!

323
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,355
It's genius.

324
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:23,691
Your grandfather's gonna be blown away.

325
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:30,572
I have a present for my future CEO.

326
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:35,202
-Oh my God. It's perfect.
-Yeah?

327
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:36,578
I love you, babe.

328
00:16:37,871 --> 00:16:40,666
The pick-me energy in this room…

329
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:45,045
Josh knows
it's not just a one-person race anymore.

330
00:16:46,213 --> 00:16:48,215
Did you see the look on my brother's face?

331
00:16:48,298 --> 00:16:50,300
[both laughing]

332
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:55,305
Oh… Richard tried his hardest
to keep me in the mail room.

333
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:59,351
But I worked my way up.

334
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,061
And you will too.

335
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:03,647
If I take over for Uncle Sterling,

336
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:07,901
and you stay VP,
then we'll outnumber Richard two to one.

337
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:10,029
Keep it up, kid.

338
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,408
[urgent music playing]

339
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:16,744
911. Josh invited Cabrera.

340
00:17:18,412 --> 00:17:21,331
-Oh, and she brought Fry Guy.
-If Quaid sees him, he's going to flip.

341
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:25,377
Nice to see you, boys.

342
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:26,587
-Teagan.
-Hi.

343
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:28,005
Where is Josh?

344
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:31,842
It was so thoughtful of him
to invite the school rowing committee.

345
00:17:31,925 --> 00:17:33,635
Oh, he's over there.

346
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:35,888
Oh, thank you.

347
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,601
-Hey, that's mine.
-Mine now.

348
00:17:41,602 --> 00:17:42,936
Cretin.

349
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:46,774
We need to find Quaid now.

350
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,984
-Come on.
-Okay, come on.

351
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:55,032
We need a plan, so let's just spread out.
Outside and exhibits and hallways.

352
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:58,494
Once we find him, we'll bring him here,
and, Crabby, you'll distract him,

353
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:02,122
and then Baloo and Cam,
you'll grab him and, uh…

354
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:04,541
throw him in here.

355
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:06,168
What? Why?

356
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:07,961
To trap him until Ethan leaves.

357
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:09,463
Great. Where do you want me?

358
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:10,547
Stop! Okay, guys.

359
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:13,759
We're not trapping Quaid,
our friend, in a closet.

360
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:15,010
-Give him a flashlight.
-Yes.

361
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:16,261
It's kidnapping, Crabby.

362
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,305
Also, have you seen him?
He's not fitting in there.

363
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:20,641
We're not doing it.
It's not fair to Quaid.

364
00:18:23,018 --> 00:18:24,353
Hey.

365
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:27,022
Guys, we all know
that there's no stopping Quaid here.

366
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,316
-There's gotta be another way.
-If we don't do this plan,

367
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:31,527
then he'll get kicked off the team,
so come on.

368
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,904
-Why should we listen?
-Because I'm the coxie and I said so!

369
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:35,906
[scoffs]

370
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:40,202
Well, I don't think so.
I'm gonna go check the party.

371
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:41,370
I'm gonna go dance.

372
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:42,704
-We're gonna…
-…go this way.

373
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:46,834
[Cam sighs]

374
00:18:49,002 --> 00:18:49,878
Oof.

375
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:51,380
Yeah, I know. I heard it.

376
00:18:51,463 --> 00:18:54,049
-I can't take that back, can I?
-It's out there.

377
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:59,138
Come on. Maybe he went this way.

378
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,565
Hey, did you have to leave me hanging?

379
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:13,318
-I wasn't gonna manhandle Quaid.
-I was doing it for the team, you know.

380
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,821
You don't know what it actually means
to be on a crew.

381
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:19,074
Okay, well, explain it.

382
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:20,701
It's like a brotherhood.

383
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:24,788
We don't have to like each other.
We look out for one another.

384
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:27,833
But they don't look out for you.

385
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:29,168
[Cam] It's complicated.

386
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:32,254
If anyone picked a fight with me,
they'd have my back.

387
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:34,256
And I'd have theirs.

388
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:39,052
If you don't have their backs,
they're never going to listen.

389
00:19:39,136 --> 00:19:41,471
Boy bonding is so strange.

390
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:43,932
I say we forget about them
and start our own team.

391
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:44,892
-Oh yeah?
-Mm-hmm.

392
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:45,934
And just be a pair?

393
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,477
It's a lot less drama.

394
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:49,104
Or just really concentrated drama.

395
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:55,110
Hey, I would be great in a pair.
I can compromise. I can get in sync.

396
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:58,030
But I get to lead.

397
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:58,989
There it is.

398
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:05,787
Where are the bartenders or the servers?

399
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:07,831
No one's cleaning up the messes.

400
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:11,335
Someone's raiding the bar.
Hey, what are you doing?

401
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,046
You got a corkscrew?

402
00:20:16,048 --> 00:20:18,634
Hiya! I know you don't normally
serve the food,

403
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,510
but I'm in a bind and I--

404
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:24,014
Okay, nope.
That is a me problem, not a you problem.

405
00:20:24,097 --> 00:20:27,643
Mom! There you are. Okay, don't freak out,
but there's no one working out there.

406
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:28,810
There's no food or booze.

407
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:30,687
Okay, you can't have people
rawdogging a party.

408
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,773
I know, just that
when we switched the party plans,

409
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,733
I forgot to tell the servers
about the new venue.

410
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:36,568
But they're coming though. They're coming.

411
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:41,406
They're close. I called them,
and they said they were an hour away,

412
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:43,075
and that was…

413
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:44,993
12 minutes ago. Oh God.

414
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:46,328
This is going to be a disaster.

415
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:49,790
I went to a Versace after-party once
where the booze wasn't delivered.

416
00:20:49,873 --> 00:20:53,502
It took 15 minutes before the models
turned the champagne flutes into shivs.

417
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:57,130
Okay, well, we don't have 15 minutes.
The servers won't be here by then.

418
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:58,465
At least the wine's good.

419
00:20:58,548 --> 00:21:01,593
Believe me, I would know. I helped
my favorite nanny train to be a sommelier.

420
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,804
Very impressive and illegal.

421
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:06,974
My parents are socialites.
I could get a PhD in parties.

422
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:09,977
Yours would have been killer
if you had enough servers.

423
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,272
-How would you like a job?
-A job?

424
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:17,484
Got a PhD in parties. You ever work one?
You can change in the bathroom.

425
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:21,280
-Are you nuts?
-I need all the reinforcements I can get.

426
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:22,531
And guess what?

427
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:23,699
No.

428
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:27,703
-I will hate you until I die.
-It's just till the servers get here.

429
00:21:27,786 --> 00:21:30,872
Okay, Mom, I am trying to wrangle
a team of very resistant young men.

430
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,457
I can't do it in this outfit.

431
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:35,627
I know your team needs you, okay?
But I need you more.

432
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:38,755
Twenty-six hours of labor. Do this for me.

433
00:21:42,592 --> 00:21:46,972
Before every race, I take two waffles,
smash a fried egg in the middle.

434
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:51,435
But the real trick is, you fold in
a bacon croissant for extra fiber.

435
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:53,353
Yum.

436
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:55,772
[intense music playing]

437
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:56,857
What?

438
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:59,568
She was there, like,
I dunno, but she's pretty cute.

439
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:03,071
If you'll excuse me,
I have important business to attend to.

440
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:06,325
We'll see, but…

441
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:14,374
[band playing bossa nova]

442
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:20,172
I must say, I am thrilled to be interning
with Regis Airlines this summer.

443
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:22,632
I'll be working
alongside my Uncle Sterling.

444
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:24,551
You two went to college together, right?

445
00:22:24,634 --> 00:22:25,677
[Perry laughing]

446
00:22:25,761 --> 00:22:28,597
-Love the retro look.
-Can I get a hot towel, miss?

447
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:30,557
And some pretzels. Not if they're salty.

448
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,934
-Is that a caviar?
-Guys, leave some for the real guests.

449
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:36,271
-Better listen to her. She's the coxie.
-Oh my God, she's the boss of us?

450
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:38,190
Hey, that's too many cookies.

451
00:22:38,273 --> 00:22:40,025
[Perry, mouth full]
That's too many cookies.

452
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:43,403
That's a good cookie.

453
00:22:44,446 --> 00:22:46,323
Hey, I was trying to help you guys.

454
00:22:46,406 --> 00:22:48,658
-We didn't need your help. We found Quaid.
-What?

455
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:51,703
We stashed him there with that cute girl
so he wouldn't run into Ethan.

456
00:22:52,662 --> 00:22:53,663
Really?

457
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:55,874
So where is he now?

458
00:22:59,127 --> 00:23:00,420
I'll take that.

459
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,506
Philistine.

460
00:23:06,343 --> 00:23:08,345
[guests grumbling]

461
00:23:08,929 --> 00:23:11,348
Here, here, here.

462
00:23:11,431 --> 00:23:12,849
We've been waiting 15 minutes.

463
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:17,020
Okay, well, I will save you
a trip back to the bar.

464
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:23,068
Kobe beef sliders, New Zealand
grass-fed lamb lollipops, wing tips.

465
00:23:23,151 --> 00:23:27,572
One… one at a time. Some people
will claw your face for a tartare.

466
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:31,034
-Makes 'em malleable.
-[man] Lovely.

467
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:33,662
There's power here. I like this job thing.

468
00:23:33,745 --> 00:23:35,664
Good luck with the shivs.

469
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:38,583
Need a copilot?

470
00:23:42,295 --> 00:23:44,423
[playing soft bossa nova]

471
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:53,306
Hey, single malt neat. You know I got you.

472
00:23:53,390 --> 00:23:55,684
Pour yourself one
when you're finished working bar.

473
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:59,104
Wait. Why are you working the bar?

474
00:23:59,187 --> 00:24:00,564
Uh…

475
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:01,773
Oh.

476
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:03,859
Oh.

477
00:24:03,942 --> 00:24:05,527
Don't do… Don't do it.

478
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:08,738
Did you know
that this man makes a mean margarita?

479
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:11,450
I do love a margarita.

480
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:12,617
[laughs]

481
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:13,702
Yeah?

482
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:17,831
I've, uh, never seen
an event planner work the bar.

483
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:21,376
Oh. It's just until, uh…

484
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:25,797
Until now. [laughs]

485
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:26,882
Ah.

486
00:24:26,965 --> 00:24:28,383
[quietly] Thank God.

487
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:31,887
Well, everyone's raving
about the canapés and the wine.

488
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,138
Well done.

489
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:37,058
I bet my wife hires you for Halloween
and our anniversary party too.

490
00:24:42,981 --> 00:24:44,816
[laughing]

491
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:51,072
[Teagan] What are you doing?

492
